etym:
/*opokimi/ → /*oɸokimi/ → /owokimi/ → /ookimi/ → /oːkimi/.
Compound of Old Japanese elements 大(おお) (ō, “great, big, large”) + 君(きみ) (kimi, “lord, lady”).
In the pronunciation ōgimi, the kimi changes to gimi as an instance of rendaku (連濁).

